Interstellar is a science-fiction film directed by Christopher Nolan, released in 2014. The story follows Cooper, a former NASA pilot and engineer who lives on a future Earth where environmental changes are threatening humanity's survival. When he discovers a secret NASA mission, he joins a team of astronauts tasked with traveling through a wormhole in search of a habitable planet. The film stars Matthew McConaughey as Cooper, Anne Hathaway as Dr. Amelia Brand, and Jessica Chastain as the adult Murph, Cooper's daughter. The screenplay was written by Jonathan Nolan and Christopher Nolan, with the story developed by Christopher Nolan. Hans Zimmer composed the film's score. Blending space exploration with personal drama, the movie explores love, sacrifice, time dilation, gravity, and humanity's determination to survive. It was produced by Syncopy and Lynda Obst Productions. The film runs for 169 minutes and was primarily filmed in Canada, Iceland, and the United States.